ready: 1
kind: rule
id: trust.rule.input-gate
display_id: RULE-TRUST-GATE
module: trust
title: Whether a memory change applies, waits for review, or is quarantined
summary: >-
  Decides whether a memory change applies now, waits for review, or is quarantined, based on what
  supports it.
notes: >-
  Behavior-changing memories with only outside support are quarantined, preferences need the
  person's own words, and owner or protected content never changes automatically.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/trust/gate.rs::decide
inputs:
- name: proposal
  source: The proposed change, its memory kind and belief type, and its derived tier
  source_kind: derived
- name: target
  source: The target memory's latest author and whether it is protected
  source_kind: stored
- name: requester
  source: 'Who asked for the change: a deliberate call, processing, sleep, an import, or sync'
  source_kind: parameter
rules:
- trust.rule.source-tier
sets:
- name: behavior-changing kinds
  members:
  - guardrail
  - playbook
  - value
  - belief of type preference
  - belief of type rule
  - belief of type principle
  - belief of type strategy
decision:
  nodes:
  - id: in
    node_kind: input
    text: A proposed memory change with its kind, tier, and target
  - id: owner
    node_kind: decision
    text: Does it change a memory whose latest version the owner wrote, or a protected memory?
  - id: third
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is it a behavior-changing kind supported only by outside content?
  - id: pref
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is it a preference without any of the person's own words as support?
  - id: deliberate
    node_kind: decision
    text: Did the agent ask for it with a deliberate memory call?
  - id: hold-owner
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Hold for review because it would change the owner's content
  - id: quarantine
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Quarantine for review, marked as supported only by outside content
  - id: hold-pref
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Hold for review because the person never stated the preference
  - id: apply-marked
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Apply, recorded with the agent-inferred tier
  - id: apply
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Apply now
  edges:
  - from: in
    to: owner
  - from: owner
    to: hold-owner
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: owner
    to: third
    label: 'No'
  - from: third
    to: quarantine
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: third
    to: pref
    label: 'No'
  - from: pref
    to: hold-pref
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: pref
    to: deliberate
    label: 'No'
  - from: deliberate
    to: apply-marked
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: deliberate
    to: apply
    label: 'No'
precedence:
- The first matching hold wins; quarantine is checked before the preference hold.
default: Apply now
rationale: |-
  Quarantine blocks the persistent prompt-injection path without blocking memories of things that actually happened, because outcomes the agent observed carry the first-party tier.

  Preferences need the person's words because an agent inferring what its owner likes, then acting on it every session, is how memory drifts away from the person it serves.

  A deliberate agent call still applies, since the agent decides what it remembers, but it keeps the agent-inferred tier so recall shows it as the agent's own inference rather than as fact.
